- getPresentPropositions() builds a new TreeSet for every predecessor, but the result depends only on this. Compute it once before the loop.
- isSafetyAcc() calls getNextSet() again; it could reuse the precomputed set fr
- All transitions into a node share the same propositions, so lf.makeLabel(...) produces the same string for each of them. Compute the label once per node instead of once per edge.

